fix(scripts): tell an unreachable log apart from a failed check (#281)

verify-branch.sh matched exit 0, 4 and 5 by name and swept everything else
into its failure bucket. `innsegl verify` exits 6 on a configuration it
cannot verify with, so an ordinary commit run through an unconfigured
verifier came out as "claim(s) an agent identity that does not hold" — an
accusation of forgery levelled at a commit nothing had looked at. doc 06 P2
forbids that collapse, and it is the collapse that teaches people REFUSED
means --no-verify.

Exit 6, and any status the gate does not recognise, is now UNCHECKABLE: it
still fails the gate, with its own exit status and its own words. Every
non-empty bucket is reported; the exit status follows precedence, failure
first.

The verifier itself was measured correct and is unchanged — with the log
unreachable it returns 4 and renders VERDICT: UNAVAILABLE, with the log up
it returns 0.

Driven by verify-branch-selftest.sh case 4, watched failing against the
pre-change gate: "an unconfigured verifier returned 3 — a commit nothing
looked at, called a forgery (doc 06 P2)".

The selftest could not have caught this, and is fixed alongside:

- It needs both URLs and never checked; unconfigured, every case measured
  case 4 and three of them reported it as a failure of something else. It
  now refuses up front and says what to export. The documented Rekor port
  was stale.
- Its pinned fixture had rotted — the deployment has been re-keyed since,
  so the certificate no longer chains and the current log holds no entry.
  Measured: the fixture failed checks 1 and 2 unforged, so case 2 had been
  going red with no forgery in it. Re-pinned, and the pin is now verified
  before anything forges it, telling a rotted pin from a deployment that is
  down.
- Case 3 gated 164 real commits and asserted the whole range was
  inconclusive. The rotted fixture sat inside it and genuinely failed, so
  the gate correctly returned 3 and the case reported a P2 collapse that
  was not there. It now gates one commit, already known to verify, and
  moves only the Rekor URL.
- Case 4 is new, and each case carries a comment saying what it proves.

Measured under sh and bash: 4 passed, 0 failed.

